<!--Render Target Documentation — SettingsFormat
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.SettingsFormat-->
<rdoc:SettingsFormat xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    SettingsBundle plus emitter, pseudo-map in V1
  </is>
  <documentation>
    The V3 library passes instance parameters via a settings argument on
    mb_block and reads them with mb_param(config, settings, key, default) and
    mb_param_size (and the other mb_param_* getters). The renderer supports two
    emission formats. Only one is active at runtime.

    V1 — pseudo-map (the only format the current library understands):

        mb_block(
            config = mb_config,
            settings = [
                ["size", size],
                ["brick1SizeY", brick1SizeY]
            ]
        );

    Future — OpenSCAD native object() when that type is stable:

        settings = object(
            size = size,
            brick1SizeY = brick1SizeY
        )

    Nested composition settings would become nested objects. Today's equivalent
    is separate mb_block() calls with a flat settings list per call, not nested
    pair arrays.

    Two layers, so composition logic never hardcodes pseudo-map syntax:

    1. Resolve properties to a SettingsBundle (renderer-neutral).
       Map of scadName to SCAD expression text.
       Built from PropertyResolver: inline, then preset, then config, then default.
    2. SettingsEmitter turns the bundle into the settings argument expression.
       PseudoMapSettingsEmitter is the V1 default.
       ObjectSettingsEmitter is future.

        interface SettingsBundle {
          entries: ReadonlyMap of string to string
        }
        interface SettingsEmitter {
          emit(bundle: SettingsBundle): string
        }

    Rules:

    - Property resolution is format-agnostic. The same bundle feeds both emitters.
    - Only the emitter changes when the format changes.
    - The composition renderer calls emitter.emit(childBundle) per mb_block().
    - Nested mb_block() trees stay structurally identical.
    - The switch is target-level config, not per property.

        interface ScadRenderOptions {
          settingsFormat?: "pseudo-map" | "object"
        }

    Wired from CompileOptions / targetOptions.machineblocks-v3-scad.
    V1 rejects object with diagnostic BML_SETTINGS_FORMAT_UNSUPPORTED and
    writes no file while the SCAD library cannot read it.

    Migration when object() is stable: the SCAD library gains object-aware
    getters; ObjectSettingsEmitter lands in this package; settingsFormat object
    is opt-in, then default; PseudoMapSettingsEmitter stays for older OpenSCAD.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:PropertyRenderer" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:SettingsFormat>
